+`POST /stories` and `DELETE /stories/<id>` take `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, where the token is env `POSTILLA_AUTHOR_TOKEN`, compared in constant time: both are hashed with SHA-256 and the digests compared, so neither the token's length nor its bytes leak. The scheme `Bearer` is matched case-insensitively and followed by one space. The route (path and method) is matched first, then the token, then the body: an unknown path or method is a 404 with no token check, and a missing or wrong token gets a 401 with an empty body, before the body is read; the server then closes the connection, so the unread body is never taken for a request. `GET /stories`, `GET /genres`, `GET /tags`, `GET /authors` and `GET /languages` are public.
 
